From 61daa2a2af52648c5b2e3fae690c8ac664a9de5c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 06:42:55 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(post): keep a repeated tool in the grbl-family posts

grblhal.cps, grbl.cps and tinyg.cps remember the tool that the program
last loaded. A section that asks for the same tool writes no T M6
(grblHAL, TinyG) and no tool-change M0 (Grbl 1.1). A program stop or an
optional stop after an operation makes the tool unknown again. The Z
lift, the spindle words and the clearance traverse stay.

Pinned by crates/post/tests/grbl_family_same_tool.rs.

Fixes #3445

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
